WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:08.090
As we get closer day by day to the much overdue
removal of Donald Trump, we have to start

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:16.180
seriously addressing the question of how to
deprogram nearly 75 million Trump.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.060
This is not a trivial matter.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.130
This is not easy to do.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:23.710
I've said before Trump will go, but the Trump
ists will still be here.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:27.029
The Trump ism that has become their sort of
guiding.

00:00:27.029 --> 00:00:31.109
I don't want to say guiding principles because
it's not very principle, but their guiding

00:00:31.109 --> 00:00:33.320
ideology that will be here.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:34.449
So how do we do it?

00:00:34.449 --> 00:00:36.760
How do we deprogram these people?

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:42.699
A retail strategy of convincing individuals
that their views are misguided is just too

00:00:42.699 --> 00:00:43.699
time consuming.

00:00:43.699 --> 00:00:47.920
I had this caller to my show last week who
said, David, I did it.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:49.579
I'd programed one Trump.

00:00:49.579 --> 00:00:52.159
And I said, well, how long did it take?

00:00:52.159 --> 00:00:53.600
And the guy said, it took three hours.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.149
So as you can see, three hours time, 75 million.

00:00:57.149 --> 00:00:58.559
That's a problem.

00:00:58.559 --> 00:00:59.559
All right.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.660
It's easy and popular to say education's the
solution.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:03.989
We have to improve education.

00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:07.369
Well, we do, but that's not going to help
people already out of school.

00:01:07.369 --> 00:01:11.869
There's no doubt that teaching, critical thinking,
media literacy, epistemology starting when

00:01:11.869 --> 00:01:19.430
kids are 10, 11, 12, that would preemptively
insulate a lot of Americans from being brought

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:21.729
into these cult mentalities.

00:01:21.729 --> 00:01:25.619
But we're talking about seventy five million
people mostly who are already out of school.

00:01:25.619 --> 00:01:28.030
So fixing education won't fix them.

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:31.640
So what do you do if you research cults?

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:37.829
You very quickly learn that forcibly removing
people is not recommended.

00:01:37.829 --> 00:01:39.100
It rarely works.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:45.020
You need to get people to a place where they
choose to leave the cult voluntarily.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:50.479
What we do know is that Socratic methods of
questioning, asking people what attracted

00:01:50.479 --> 00:01:55.799
you to the cult, what was going on in your
life when you know you don't want to necessarily

00:01:55.799 --> 00:01:56.799
use the word cult here.

00:01:56.799 --> 00:02:00.979
But when when you started to say, hey, I think
Trump has something for me, what was going

00:02:00.979 --> 00:02:01.979
on in your life?

00:02:01.979 --> 00:02:03.229
What attracted you to it?

00:02:03.229 --> 00:02:06.119
How would you know if the leader was lying?

00:02:06.119 --> 00:02:11.050
What would it mean to you if you realized
that the leader was misleading you?

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:13.110
How would you react?

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:16.459
That type of Socratic interviewing and questioning
can be useful.

00:02:16.459 --> 00:02:20.090
But again, we are talking small scale cults
here.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:25.489
We are dealing with seventy five million people
who are regularly being programed by Fox News

00:02:25.489 --> 00:02:29.540
and Rush Limbaugh and the Republican Party
and others, and they're being pulled further

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:31.200
into the cult.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.720
So it's not looking great so far.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:40.650
One idea is that their beliefs and illusions
have to have consequences that they link to

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:41.650
their beliefs.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:43.780
And that last part is very key.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:49.250
Obviously, Trump cultism has led to more coronavirus
deaths than we needed to have.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:52.050
We have we are worse off as far as health
care goes.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:57.569
Our foreign policy is is materially worse
because of Trump ism and the Trump cult and

00:02:57.569 --> 00:02:58.569
Trump.

00:02:58.569 --> 00:03:00.879
So there are consequences to Trump ism.

00:03:00.879 --> 00:03:06.709
But your average cultist will never link the
consequences to their cult leader, in this

00:03:06.709 --> 00:03:07.910
case, Donald Trump.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:14.299
So one idea is actually seeing and feeling
the consequences of their beliefs could be

00:03:14.299 --> 00:03:15.650
a start.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.349
But how do you do that?

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:24.370
How you do it when we don't even have agreement
about the basic facts is a real problem.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:30.200
And this, as you can probably tell, is such
an overwhelming Herculean task that it's likely

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:34.340
going to require multiple components and a
sort of full court press approach.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:35.560
So education.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:36.780
Yes.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:42.050
More education for young people, but that
is going to deal with people who are mostly

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:46.349
not yet voters, we need to do something about
current cultists.

00:03:46.349 --> 00:03:51.099
Do you have to look at the FCC and look at
what can and should be done from a regulatory

00:03:51.099 --> 00:03:53.060
standpoint in terms of media?

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.909
Yeah, I guess so.

00:03:54.909 --> 00:04:01.269
But I don't think you're going to solve this
problem by banning Fox News and you run into

00:04:01.269 --> 00:04:04.730
some real problems with regard to suppression
of speech when you do that.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:07.950
So I don't know how big of a part that's going
to play.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:14.569
Another big part of this is we need to make
it less appealing to be part of the cult.

00:04:14.569 --> 00:04:19.780
Lots of people get drawn into cults and conspiracy
theories in the first place because they either

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:25.480
find the cults in conspiracies better than
the alternative of the real world or because

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:30.700
people are isolated and they get a feeling
of belonging that's really tough to pull people

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:31.700
out of.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:38.870
Of part of this is making it less seductive
to be part of the cult while recognizing the

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:41.050
underlying concerns that people have.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:46.760
And that's what Trump on purpose or accidentally
this is what Trump did do well in 2016 by

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:54.420
tricking people, Trump bamboozled people by
convincing them that he had the solutions

00:04:54.420 --> 00:05:01.200
to their problems, a fear that a lot of white
voters had of losing a privileged status in

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.200
society.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:06.730
Trump said he would take care of that immigrants
as the reason that you aren't making more

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:07.730
money.

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:08.860
Trump said he would fix it.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:15.380
So part of the deprogramming has to be acknowledging
people's concerns, but making them realize

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:20.660
that they've been sold the wrong solutions
are really, really important aspect of this.

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:26.940
And even if we do all of this, we have to
realize that change is slow unless it's a

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:29.870
completely authoritarian dystopia.

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:34.880
If you consider that the start of this cult
that we see today could have been the welfare

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:39.400
queens stories of Ronald Reagan's presidency
35 years ago.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:42.630
And you understand that this has been 35 years
in the making.

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:45.830
It no longer is reasonable to think we're
going to get out of it very quickly.

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:47.060
It's going to take time.

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:52.430
If you consider the start of the current Republican
cultism to be the civil rights movement of

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:57.120
the 1960s, then, you know, if it took 50 years
to get into the 60 years to get into this

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.990
is going to take a while to get out.

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:05.590
One of the faster programmings we've ever
seen or better said, maybe reprograming was

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:07.990
in China during the Cultural Revolution.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:11.720
Under Mao Zedong, it was a roughly 10 year
period.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:17.730
The left overs of capitalism were purged and
it was done brutally and quickly and quickly,

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:18.880
still meant a decade.

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:23.040
So what I want people to understand is this
isn't going to happen overnight.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:30.100
The fastest reprograming have been brutal
and horrifying, like the 10 year Cultural

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:32.340
Revolution in China.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:37.110
The path will be very long and it typically
requires the type of commitment that two,

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:42.120
four and six year political terms, which is
what we see in the House, White House and

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:44.810
Senate to foreign six years.

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:50.170
That's not a timeline that incentivizes the
difficult work that needs to be done.

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:52.250
So send me your thoughts.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:53.340
Send me your ideas.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:59.540
This is going to be a very, very long fight,
which it can start the day we decide it starts.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:02.550
I believe it has already started to some degree.

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:03.550
Send me your thoughts.

00:07:03.550 --> 00:08:16.910
I'm on Twitter at David Pakman,

